        "specs": {
          "when": {
            "id": ["project-detail-en-2", "project-detail-ru-2", "projects-en-3", "projects-ru-3"]
          },
          "add": ["wtb-text--specs"],
          "note": "a spec sheet: every item's title is a short label (Client, Region, Area, Duration) and the value under it is the bold line — the reverse of a feature list. CSS `.wtb-text--specs` in sections.css. Not Dividends (investor-relations-*-7) or Indicative pricing (services-*-6): there the title IS the bold value. Not Key figures (investor-relations-*-4): that is a four-column table the extractor cannot carry as items, it must stay verbatim"
        },
        "ink": {
          "when": {
            "id": ["investor-relations-en-7", "investor-relations-ru-7"]
          },
          "add": ["wtb-text--ink"],
          "note": "Dividends: an ink band (#14171a) in the source — paper title, lede in the band grey, priced rows with white values. CSS `.wtb-text--ink` in sections.css (written full-1, hooked full-2). Named by id: the project detail opening sheet is ink too but through `media-end` + `specs` together, and every other text section sits on paper or the warm surface"
        },
        "card": {
          "when": {
            "id": ["about-en-9", "about-ru-9"]
          },
          "add": ["wtb-text--card"],
          "note": "Safety (D23.3): in the source not a split but a small beige card — border, 28px padding, title clamp(22px, 2.5vw, 28px), 16/1.68 copy, a 200px image box after the copy — the second column of the Accreditations grid (source section 1051, which the spec-pack cut in two: about-*-8 verbatim, about-*-9 typed). The class is the hook; its rules belong in assets/css/sections.css. \"Beside\" cannot come from a class on this section alone: the two halves are sibling blocks, so either the spec keeps 1051 whole or the page grid pairs them"
        }
      }
    },
    "links": {
      "pattern": "wp-tracy-business/section-links",
      "root": ".wtb-links",
      "item": "links.item.<n>",
      "fields": {
        "eyebrow": {
          "block": "core/paragraph",
          "path": "links.eyebrow",
          "attr": "content",
          "repeat": null
        },
        "heading": {
          "block": "core/heading",
          "path": "links.heading",
          "attr": "content",
          "repeat": null
        },
        "headingLevel": {
          "block": "core/heading",
          "path": "links.heading",
          "attr": "level",
          "repeat": null
        },
        "intro": {
          "block": "core/paragraph",
          "path": "links.intro",
          "attr": "content",
          "repeat": null
        },
        "items.title": {
          "block": "core/paragraph",
          "path": "links.item.<n>.title",
          "attr": "content",
          "repeat": "items"
        },
        "items.text": {
          "block": "core/paragraph",
          "path": "links.item.<n>.text",
          "attr": "content",
          "repeat": "items"
        },
        "items.meta": {
          "block": "core/paragraph",
          "path": "links.item.<n>.meta",
          "attr": "content",
          "repeat": "items"
        },
        "items.href": {
          "block": "core/paragraph",
          "path": "links.item.<n>.title",
          "attr": "href",
          "repeat": "items",
          "note": "the title is the link"
        }
      },
      "note": "untyped sections detected by shape: a container of ≥2 <a> rows with at most one leading label; each row → item (title = link text, meta = trailing text, href)",
      "shape": "links",
      "styles": {
        "files": {
          "when": {
            "id": ["investor-relations-en-5#1", "investor-relations-ru-5#1"]
          },
          "add": ["wtb-links--files"],
          "note": "Reports and presentations: the rows are downloads in the source — title 600, an orange ↓ after the title — where the disclosures list under it (investor-relations-*-6) keeps 500 with the same markup. A shape-detected section renders as `<moduleId>#<group>` (seed.mjs renderTypedEntry), so the id carries the group suffix. CSS `.wtb-links--files` in sections.css (written full-1, hooked full-2)"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
